    {
      "id": "s3",
      "caption": "The p-value trap: it is not P(H₀ is true)",
      "narration": "A p-value of 0.03 does not mean there is a 3 percent chance the null is true. It means: if the null were true, only 3 percent of experiments would produce data this extreme. The p-value is about the data given the null, not about the null itself.",
